  - T1: a number in concentration_value next to a regulatory field counts as a result only if the result cell itself printed something. This is decided by
    which fields are filled, never by comparing values. It catches the extractor copying the reference into the number.
  - T2: you said to keep the declared-absent logic as is. I did change it in one way: it no longer applies to Class 1/2A, because ICH Q3D assesses those
    classes whether or not they're intentionally added. Class 2B/3 exclusion is unchanged, so there are still no phantom 2B/3 values.
  - T5: "as per USP <467>" directly before a number makes it a reference. "Methanol (as per USP <467>): NMT 3000 ppm" stays the material's spec, because an
    NMT after a citation is a spec citing its standard.

